        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Systems come in many forms. Some are rigid, with fixed boundaries and strict coupling between components. Others are elastic, stretching under pressure but returning to their original shape."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "The key insight is that constraints are not inherently limiting. Without constraints there is no structure, and without structure there is no evolution."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "element",
      "name": "p",
      "attributes": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "This taxonomy helps us understand different system architectures and their resilience characteristics."
        }
